    "PLO5"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>TypYou are developing a university management system in Java. You need to retrieve student data based on department and marks using <strong data-end=\"4201\" data-start=\"4193\">JDBC</strong>, and you must use <strong data-end=\"4247\" data-start=\"4220\">declarative SQL queries</strong> within an <strong data-end=\"4287\" data-start=\"4258\">imperative JDBC structure</strong>. You also need to explain the JDBC architecture behind this process.</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"4410\" data-start=\"4363\">Write Java code to do the following:</p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"4626\" data-start=\"4411\">\n\t<li data-end=\"4431\" data-start=\"4411\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4431\" data-start=\"4413\">Load JDBC driver</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4456\" data-start=\"4432\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4456\" data-start=\"4434\">Establish connection</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4534\" data-start=\"4457\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4534\" data-start=\"4459\">Retrieve names and scores of students in &#39;CSE&#39; department with marks &gt; 75</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4626\" data-start=\"4535\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4626\" data-start=\"4537\">Close all resources<br data-end=\"4559\" data-start=\"4556\" />\n\tAlso, explain which parts are declarative and which are imperative.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
